SWEET ACM and AKS: the kernel PRNG for ids and salts, and room for 256 contexts (2323b)

ast247 showed the Set Passcode sheet for the first time, and every
ACMContextCreate on the phone still failed, now with -4 (it was -5 with no
service). The cause is the RNG, not the protocol. Both shims called
random_buf(), which is cc_rand_generate(), which answers -1 unless the corecrypto
kext has registered g_crypto_funcs. SWEET loads no kexts and its own PRNG
registers only the cckprng (osfmk/prng/prng_random.c), so on this kernel
random_buf() fails on every call. acm_random() then zeroed the id, the store
refused the all-zero id four times and cmd_create() answered SACM_ERR_NOMEM, -4.
ACMLib returns that kernel status unchanged (LocalAuthenticationCore
_performCommand 0x1b23503f8, ManagedConfiguration's copy 0x1a93d6ba0), so every
caller logged "ACMContextCreate failed: -4". The host tests never saw it because
their random_buf() stand-ins always succeeded.

The same call fed 2321's salt: every passcode record written on SWEET so far had
a 16-byte all-zero salt. Records keep their salt, so old ones still verify.

- SweetACM.cpp acm_random() and SweetKeyStore.cpp pc_io_random() call
  read_random(), the kernel PRNG itself. It cannot fail (a DRBG error panics).
  The store still refuses an all-zero or repeated id.
- SACM_MAX 64 -> 256. With create working, every LocalAuthentication client can
  hold 16 contexts until it exits, and four of them would leave profiled none
  (audit-acm-report.md, non-blocking finding 3). Per connection stays 16.

Nothing else changes: the wire format, the entitlement gate, task pinning,
ownership, selector 15's resolution and 2324's stage and commit are untouched.

Needs 2321, 2322 and 2323. 2324 applies on top unchanged (offsets only).
Audit brief: plans/passcode/audit-brief-acm2.md.

Check: python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-acm.py XNU_DIR
       python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-2phase.py XNU_DIR
       python3 -I plans/passcode/tools/check-lock.py XNU_DIR
Apply: git apply -p1 in the kernel tree, after 2323 and before 2324.
